iv> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll admit I can usually only watch a couple episodes of Mr. Pickles before I have to leave the room.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you feel about Super Jail?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T10:52:41-07:00","id":1066455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1065096-mr-pickles-and-the-wyrm?p=1066154#post1066154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How do you feel about Super Jail?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have never heard of Super Jail. *googles*<br /> <br /> On the surface is seems like a Pentex run Prison gone wrong (or right if you are of the Wyrm).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T10:54:04-07:00","id":1066456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1065096-mr-pickles-and-the-wyrm?p=1066123#post1066123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is nothing wrong with that format, as long as your players understand what comes with advancing in Rank personality-wise. I've had some players that couldn't wrap their head around it and at Rank 2 were still trying to do the dumb things cubs do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but with certain players, you'd have the same issue if you advance rank via Renown points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T13:00:49-07:00","id":1066536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1065096-mr-pickles-and-the-wyrm?p=1066456#post1066456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but with certain players, you'd have the same issue if you advance rank via Renown points.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly. Just speaking from my experience though, not as much. Since Renown takes time and stories to accrue, the players (for newer players) and characters tend to mature some as the storylines advance.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T13:14:26-07:00","id":1066540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1065096-mr-pickles-and-the-wyrm?p=1066536#post1066536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Possibly. Just speaking from my experience though, not as much. Since Renown takes time and stories to accrue, the players (for newer players) and characters tend to mature some as the storylines advance.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you are at most going to get a good year out of a game before everyone grows bored and moves on, you would want to increase the rate of advancement. <br /> <br /> It's a balancing act between giving your players time to mature into the character and hoping real life or boredom doesn't end the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T16:55:31-07:00","id":1066640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1065096-mr-pickles-and-the-wyrm?p=1066540#post1066540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you are at most going to get a good year out of a game before everyone grows bored and moves on, you would want to increase the rate of advancement.<br /> <br /> It's a balancing act between giving your players time to mature into the character and hoping real life or boredom doesn't end the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. And it's not usually easy to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T06:55:33-07:00","id":1066831,"title":"","content":"I have seen entire groups get demoted a Rank because they went along with the stupidity of another party member, but that is how the system is designed to function. If PCs do not want to deal with the Renown system, they really do not want to play Garou (or any Fera really). Unlike with mortals, Glory, Honor, and Wisdom (and their equivalents) mean something to the Garou and the Fera.<br /> <br /> I think that there are just some PCs who want to play games where their actions have no consequences. They want to be the Karma Houdini, the evil bastard who gets away with everything and dies fat and happy at an extreme old age, and they really hate it when STs and gamelines try to enforce consequences for their actions. They are the type of people who will not join a game because you will not let them make a serial killer as a party member and will leave a game because you have the police kicking down their door the day after their character casually goes on a shooting spree in a strip mall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T07:17:34-07:00","id":1066852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1065096-mr-pickles-and-the-wyrm?p=1066831#post1066831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have seen entire groups get demoted a Rank because they went along with the stupidity of another party member, but that is how the system is designed to function. If PCs do not want to deal with the Renown system, they really do not want to play Garou (or any Fera really). Unlike with mortals, Glory, Honor, and Wisdom (and their equivalents) mean something to the Garou and the Fera.<br /> <br /> I think that there are just some PCs who want to play games where their actions have no consequences. They want to be the Karma Houdini, the evil bastard who gets away with everything and dies fat and happy at an extreme old age, and they really hate it when STs and gamelines try to enforce consequences for their actions. They are the type of people who will not join a game because you will not let them make a serial killer as a party member and will leave a game because you have the police kicking down their door the day after their character casually goes on a shooting spree in a strip mall.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm not talking about ignoring the renown system. If the PCs do something stupid there will be renown consequences.<br /> <br /> I'm suggesting that you ignore the in game Renown point system. Just progress Renown based on plot. Use the chart as a guide, but don't keep track of the points themselves. I assume Renown points are a gaming mechanic rather than something a character worries about in game. It's not like a Glasswalker has a Renown App to keep track of his points and curses when he is two points short and won't be joining the rest of his pack on their Fostern Challenge.<br /> <br /> Note, as both an ST and a Player, I lean towards Rules light. My plots involve political and ethical dilemmas. If it is time for the players and plot to progressive to Fostern/Adren level storylines, I'm not going to stat up a bunch of random banes in an effort to make makes sure my players have enough Renown to move on to the next plot. I rather just have a time skip where it is assumed the characters kill bane number 390 to get that last point of Glory. If the players screw up and lose renown in the eyes of the Garou Nation, well that is more plot for me to work with.<br /> <br /> I understand my play style makes the number crunchers twitch. Just like your crazy Garou/Dragonblooded baby factory math makes me twitch. We each have our own play styles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 03-23-2017, 10:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T08:27:07-07:00","id":1066896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1065096-mr-pickles-and-the-wyrm?p=1066831#post1066831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that there are just some PCs who want to play games where their actions have no consequences. They want to be the Karma Houdini, the evil bastard who gets away with everything and dies fat and happy at an extreme old age, and they really hate it when STs and gamelines try to enforce consequences for their actions. They are the type of people who will not join a game because you will not let them make a serial killer as a party member and will leave a game because you have the police kicking down their door the day after their character casually goes on a shooting spree in a strip mall.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have had players like that. I don't really put up with them anymore. Some folks only seem to be capable of interfacing with make-believe worlds using violence, and I kinda find that half-sad, half-scary. Even in a game as messy as Werewolf, there are people and things you don't want to kill, and some players hate accepting the consequences of their bloodthirsty actions.<br /> <br /> I have found that everyone is usually happier if the psycho ends up playing out their ultraviolent tendencies in GTA rather than WtA.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1065096-mr-pickles-and-the-wyrm?p=1066852#post1066852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not talking about ignoring the renown system. If the PCs do something stupid there will be renown consequences.<br /> <br /> I'm suggesting that you ignore the in game Renown point system. Just progress Renown based on plot. Use the chart as a guide, but don't keep track of the points themselves. I assume Renown points are a gaming mechanic rather than something a character worries about in game. It's not like a Glasswalker has a Renown App to keep track of his points and curses when he is two points short and won't be joining the rest of his pack on their Fostern Challenge.<br /> <br /> Note, as both an ST and a Player, I lean towards Rules light. My plots involve political and ethical dilemmas. If it is time for the players and plot to progressive to Fostern/Adren level storylines, I'm not going to stat up a bunch of random banes in an effort to make makes sure my players have enough Renown to move on to the next plot. I rather just have a time skip where it is assumed the characters kill bane number 390 to get that last point of Glory. If the players screw up and lose renown in the eyes of the Garou Nation, well that is more plot for me to work with.<br /> <br /> I understand my play style makes the number crunchers twitch. Just like your crazy Garou/Dragonblooded baby factory math makes me twitch. We each have our own play styles.</div> </div> </div> </div>A-are you me?<br /> <br /> Seriously though, after playing the game for a few years straight I have basically reached all the same conclusions, chucking the point-based renown system out the window in order to keep things more loosey-goosey. Part of that decision was motivated by time lapses where we would skip ahead several months 'off camera.' That made keeping track of individual acts pretty wonky. They are going to accrue the points over the in-game years anyway, but I am saved the headache of keeping track of every jot and tittle.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T14:05:48-07:00","id":1067164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1065096-mr-pickles-and-the-wyrm?p=1066852#post1066852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...It's not like a Glasswalker has a Renown App to keep track of his points and curses when he is two points short and won't be joining the rest of his pack on their Fostern Challenge...</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThere might not be... but there absolutely <i>should</i> be. That's <i>exactly</i> how the Glass Walkers should keep track of Renown. An app running on a fetish smartphone that constantly monitors his/her relative renown (little &quot;r&quot;) amongst the spirits at large. And (tongue-in-cheek) should be displayed in <i>precisely</i> the same abstraction terms as in-game on the character sheet.<br /> <br /> \u200bBecause there should <i>absolutely</i> be a scene where the pack slips away from a burning Pentex warehouse and as they're sneaking away, there's a loud ringtone. Everybody, pissed off, stops and turns to look at the Glass Walker, who whips out his phone. &quot;<b><i>Sh**</i></b>!!! I just lost three dots in <i>Wisdom</i>! What the <i><b>f***</b></i>!? Guys, I think we missed something. We need to go back, right now.&quot; And everybody is looking at him like &quot;What are you talking about?&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T14:27:34-07:00","id":1067177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1065096-mr-pickles-and-the-wyrm?p=1067164#post1067164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bThere might not be... but there absolutely <i>should</i> be. That's <i>exactly</i> how the Glass Walkers should keep track of Renown. An app running on a fetish smartphone that constantly monitors his/her relative renown (little &quot;r&quot;) amongst the spirits at large. And (tongue-in-cheek) should be displayed in <i>precisely</i> the same abstraction terms as in-game on the character sheet.<br /> <br /> \u200bBecause there should <i>absolutely</i> be a scene where the pack slips away from a burning Pentex warehouse and as they're sneaking away, there's a loud ringtone. Everybody, pissed off, stops and turns to look at the Glass Walker, who whips out his phone. &quot;<b><i>Sh**</i></b>!!! I just lost three dots in <i>Wisdom</i>! What the <i><b>f***</b></i>!? Guys, I think we missed something. We need to go back, right now.&quot; And everybody is looking at him like &quot;What are you talking about?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This is too funny not to have happen at least once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T17:34:23-07:00","id":1067255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1065096-mr-pickles-and-the-wyrm?p=1067164#post1067164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bThere might not be... but there absolutely <i>should</i> be. That's <i>exactly</i> how the Glass Walkers should keep track of Renown. An app running on a fetish smartphone that constantly monitors his/her relative renown (little &amp;quot;r&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> amongst the spirits at large. And (tongue-in-cheek) should be displayed in <i>precisely</i> the same abstraction terms as in-game on the character sheet.<br /> <br /> \u200bBecause there should <i>absolutely</i> be a scene where the pack slips away from a burning Pentex warehouse and as they're sneaking away, there's a loud ringtone. Everybody, pissed off, stops and turns to look at the Glass Walker, who whips out his phone. &amp;quot;<b><i>Sh**</i></b>!!! I just lost three dots in <i>Wisdom</i>! What the <i><b>f***</b></i>!? Guys, I think we missed something. We need to go back, right now.&amp;quot; And everybody is looking at him like &amp;quot;What are you talking about?&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Little does the Glasswalker know, the reason why he lost the wisdom was because he forgot to turn his fucking phone on silent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T21:27:03-07:00","id":1067387,"title":"","content":"I think that technologically minded Garou would have created fetish pocket watches capable of recording temporary Renown within the last five hundred years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}